s enterprise cloud applications in the United States and internationally. The company offers a suite of financial management applications to maintain accounting information; manage financial processes, such as payables and receivables; identify real-time financial, operational, and management insights; perform financial consolidation; reduce time-to-close; promote internal control and auditability; and achieve consistency across finance operations. It also provides spend management solutions that help organizations to streamline supplier selection and contract management, build and execute sourcing events, such as requests for proposals, and manage indirect spend; expense management solutions to submit and approve expenses; and a suite of human capital management applications that enables HR teams to hire, onboard, pay, develop, reskill, and provide employee experiences. In addition, the company offers planning applications. Further, it provides supply chain and inventory solutions to healthcare organizations; solutions to manage the end-to-end student and faculty lifecycle; Workday Extend for customers and their developers to build custom applications. The company serves the professional and business services, financial services, healthcare, manufacturing, media, education, government, technology, media, retail, and hospitality industries. It sells its solutions through its direct sales organization. The company was formerly known as North Tahoe Power Tools, Inc. and changed its name to Workday, Inc. in July 2005. Workday, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is headquartered in Pleasanton, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Aneel  Bhusri | Co-Founder, CEO & Executive Chairman of the Board | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 20K people. Revenue per employee of $457K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 29%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $133K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $78K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Workday, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $42.1B market cap on $9.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +23% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 29 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.24\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 6.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 17% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 73% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7283886807081017},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $150.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Sector under pressure with a 19.3% decline over the past 6 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Reviewing Aware (NASDAQ:AWRE) and Workday (NASDAQ:WDAY)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/reviewing-aware-nasdaqawre-and-workday-nasdaqwday.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176909.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"3,985 Shares of Workday, Inc. $WDAY Purchased by Royce & Associates LP","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/3985-shares-of-workday-inc-wday-purchased-by-royce-associates-lp.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795170891.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.863,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Workday (WDAY) Stock Dropped, So What Is Driving Attention Now?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-wday/workday/news/workday-wday-stock-dropped-so-what-is-